  "artifact_text": "**Observations**\n1. Logs from pod `billing-api-665595bbf9-dk4wf` show repeated `WARN db connection reset by peer, retrying (pool acquire 2.80s)`.\n2. Deployment record `CI-2455` shows load balancer idle timeout was changed to 120s without adjusting database idle settings.\n3. Environment variable `DB_POOL_IDLE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` on pod `billing-api-665595bbf9-dk4wf` is set to 900 seconds.\n\n**Root Cause**\nThe database connection pool idle timeout exceeds the network idle timeout threshold, causing connections closed by peers to exhaust the pool per runbook `RB-014`.\n\n**Recommended Action**\nThe backend billing team should lower `DB_POOL_IDLE_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` below the shortest network idle timeout along the path per runbook `RB-014`.\n\n**Ruled-Out Leads**\n1. An application memory leak or OOMKill was ruled out because pod conditions show continuous `Ready` status with no restarts.\n2. A deployment rollout failure was ruled out because deployment `CI-2455` completed successfully before the incident.",
